wsdl:operation.wsdl:documentation:
This method will perform a search for documents based on the specified criteria such
as title, part number or meta-data. A document is found if it matches all of the specified
criteria.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.

If either of the following occurs, then no information is returned.

 * The user does not have permission to access the categories in the briefcase.
 * The user does not have permission to access the specified custom report.

@param PartNumber, an optional part of the document's identity.
@param Title, an optional part of the document's title.
@param VersionInformation, an optional part of the document's version.
@param Published, an optional boolean value indicating whether document has been published.
@param SavedSearchId, an optional value of a previously saved search.
@param InMainBriefcase, whether to search for the document in the briefcase.
@param ReportId, an optional value of the report in which the document appears.
@param CompartmentId, an optional value of the compartment in which the document appears.
@param CategoryId, an optional value of the category in which the document appears.
@param MetaDataItem, an optional set of name/values to locate the document by.
@param License, an optional set of license values to locate the document by.
@return Results containing the PartNumber, Title, Published, URL, set of
        MetaDataItem and Filename of each document found.

This method will create a new document in the specified category.

The method will fail if:

 * The category does not exist.
 * The document is being created at a location that is too close to the root category. This
   is controlled by the 'Minimum document depth' system setting.
 * The user does not have permission to create documents.
 * The user does not have permission to assign part numbers to documents.
 * The user does not have permission to access the path to the category.
 * The part number specified for the document is not in the correct format.
 * The part number specified does not conform to that required of the specified document type.
 * The specified part number already exists.
 * No title value was specified for the new document.
 * The specified document type is invalid or does not exist.

@param CategoryID, the identity of the category in which to create the document.
@param Path, an alternative means of locating the category in the repository.
@param Title, the short description to assign to the document.
@param DocType, the type of the new document.
@param Author, the person responsible for the document's content.
@param ManualPartNumber, an optional value for the part number, that will be assigned to the
       document.
@return PartNumber containing the part number assigned to the document, either generated or
        specified with the ManualPartNumber parameter.

This method will locate one or more categories in the repository.

The method will fail if:

 * The category does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to access the category.

@param CategoryId, the optional integer identity of the category to locate.
@param Name, the optional part of the name of the category.
@param Path, the optional path to the category.
@return A collection of CatResult elements containing the ID, name, path and
        a list of child category IDs of each category located.

This method will create a new version of the document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to create issues of the specific type.
 * The user does not have permission to add new versions of the document.
 * The user does not have permission to add new issues.
 * The document is frozen and cannot be changed.
 * The document is checked-out by another user.
 * The document must be locked before a new version can be added.
 * The issue value is not in the correct format.
 * The version number for the issue is not correct.
 * The count of drafts or issues for this document has been exhausted.
 * A version of this document already exists.
 * The specified version is locked.
 * There is not enough space to store the version.
 * No content was provided for the version.
 * The filename includes an incorrect extension for the document type.
 * The supplied version number is too long.
 * The supplied version number is in the wrong format.
 * The supplied version number is before an existing one.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param IssueType, this can be either 'draft' or 'issue'.
@param IssueNumber, the version of the document.
@param IssueComment, descriptive text about the version.
@param IssueLicenseeComment, descriptive text for licensee.
@param VesionString, the version.
@param ReviewComment, descriptive text for the reviews of the new version.
@param NotificationComment, descriptive text to accompany the notification.
@param SkipPrefilter, a value of '1' stops the addition of Cognidox field data to the version.
@param MasterFile, the contents of the new version.
@param SecondaryFile, the optional contents of a file to associate with the new version.
@return IssueNumber, containing the number assigned to the submission.

This method will publish a document on the extranet if the user has sufficient
rights and the document is not already published.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to authorise the document for the extranet.
 * The user does not have permission to change the properties of the document.
 * The document has already been published.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to publish.
@param PublishComment, an optional description of why this is being published.
@param PublishLicenseeComment, an optional comment that will be visible to customers
       indicating the changes in the current document version.
@return Published, '1' if the document was published, otherwise '0'.

This method will remove a document from the extranet, if the user has sufficient
rights and the document is not already unpublished.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to authorize for extranet.
 * The user does not have permission to alter the properties of the document.
 * The document has not been published.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to unpublish.
@param UnpublishComment, an optional description as to why this is being unpublished.
@return Unpublished, '1' if the document was unpublished, otherwise '0'.

This method will check-out a document, adding a lock, so that another user
cannot make changes.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user cannot add or replace the current lock.
 * The user does not have permission to change the properties of the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to add a lock to.
@param Comment, an optional descriptive reason for the operation.
@return Locked, which has the value '1' if the document is locked.

This method will add the content bytes of a document to the repository.

The method will fail if:

 * The document's part number does not exist.
 * The 'CogniDoxKey' value was supplied and doesn't match the one on record.
 * The issue type is not one of 'issue' or 'draft'.
 * The user does not have permission to create documents or create a new version.
 * The document lock type is 'freeze' and so the document cannot be modified.
 * The document is checked-out by another user.
 * The document must be locked before a new version can be added.
 * The issue number is not in the correct format.
 * The number of drafts that can be added has been exhausted.
 * The number of issues that can be added has been exhausted.
 * A version of the document already exists.
 * The version of the document has been locked.
 * There is not enough storage for the document content.
 * No content was provided for the document submission.
 * The file name's extension was not correct for the type of the document.
 * The issue number is too long.
 * The issue number is not in the correct format.
 * The specified issue number contains a version that is before an existing one.
 * It was not possible to retrieve the current issue number of the document.

@param PartNumber, the value assigned to the document.
@param CogniDoxKey, optional value, which specifies the security key of the document.
@param IssueType, the type of the submission, either 'issue' or 'draft'.
@param IssueNumber, optional value, the number of the issue.
@param IssueComment, optional value, descriptive text about the submission.
@param IssueLicenseeComment, optional value, descriptive text about the license.
@param VersionString, optional value, a second identifier for the submission.
@param SkipPrefilter, a value of '1' stops the addition of Cognidox field data to the version.
@param MasterFilename, the name for the document file.
@param MasterFile, the base 64 encoded bytes of the document.
@param SecondaryFile, the optional contents of a file to associate with the new version.
@return IssueNumber, containing the number assigned to the submission.

This method will retrieve the actions that can be performed on a document.

The method will fail if:

 * A document does not exist with the specified part number.
 * The user is not registered with the system.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param IssueNumber, optional issue value. If missing then the latest issue is used.
@return CanOpen, CanAddDraft, CanAddIssue, CanDelete, CanRename, CanLock and a set of
        Extension values that contain the permitted file name extensions. The value
        will be either '1' or '0' depending on whether the function can be carried
        out or not by the user.

This method will change the title of the specified document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * No title value was provided.
 * Changes to the document meta-data could not be persisted.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param Title, the new value for the title of the document.
@return Title, the current title of the document. This maybe the
        same value before the change, if the modification could
        not be performed.

This method will return a collection of all the recommended titles for a given category ID.

The method will fail if:

 * The category does not exist.

If the user does not access, or is not registered, then an empty collection will be returned.

@param CategoryId, the numeric identity of the category to look up.
@param IgnoreReplacements, optional value of '1' to ignore replacement titles.
@return Titles, a collection of recommended titles consisting of the title, it's
        text and the document type it applies to.

This method will add one or more licenses to the specified document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user has limited access to the document.
 * The user does not have permission to assign licenses.
 * The user does not have permission to alter the document properties.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param LicenseComment, descriptive text about the licenses being added.
@param License, a collection of license texts to add to the document.

This method will remove one or more licenses from a document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to assign a license to documents.
 * The user does not have permission to alter the properties of the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param LicenseComment, a description explaining the removal.
@param Licenses, the set of license values to remove.

This method will create a new license token that can be assigned to licensees, documents
or categories.

The method will fail if:

 * The user does not have permission to create new licenses.
 * No value was provided for the license.
 * A license with the same value already exists.

@param License, the name of the new license.
@param Hidden, a value of '1' hides the license from view.
@return Created, with the value '1' if the license was created.

This method will add or remove agreements for the specified document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user doesn't have permission to modify the license agreements.
 * The user doesn't have permission to change the properties of the document.
 * The user is blocked from accessing the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param Comment, descriptive text for the changes to the agreements.
@param AddAgreement, a collection of agreement titles to add.
@param RemoveAgreement, a collection of agreement titles to remove.
@return Agreements, a collection of Agreement elements containing an id and
        title, of all of the document's current agreements.

This method will mark a document as current if the user has sufficient
rights and the document is currently obsolete.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to change status.
 * The user does not have permission to alter the properties of the document.
 * The document is not marked as obsolete.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to unobsolete.
@param UnobsoleteComment, an optional description to use when unobsoleting the document.
@return Unobsoleted, '1' if the document was marked as current, otherwise '0'.

This method will cancel an outstanding request for a review.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to sign off on an issue.
 * The user does not have permission to access the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param Comment, optional description about the cancellation.
@param IssueNumber, the version number of the document.
@param Invalidate, optional value, '1' to cancel and leave a record in the
       history, otherwise '0' to cancel and delete.
@return Cancelled, with the value '1' if successful, otherwise '0' if
        not.

Create a review request for a version of the specified document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * A document with the specified version does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to sign off a document version.
 * The document does not have a version that can be reviewed.
 * Reviews has been expressly forbidden.
 * The document is currently locked so no changes can be made.
 * No comment was provided for the review.
 * No due date was provided.
 * The review due date is not in the future.
 * One or more reviewers does not have access to the document.
 * At least one reviewer must review the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param IssueNumber, the version number of the document to check.
@param Comment, the review comment to send to reviewers.
@param CCReviewers, boolean to indicating whether to CC review answers.
@param ReviewDue, the GMT date for the reviews to be returned by.
@param RequestedReviewers, RequestedReviewer list of review logins.
@return Created, value of '1' indicating if the review was created and '0'
        if not.

This method will reject an approval for the specified document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to approve issues.
 * The user has not been requested to approve the document.
 * The user is blocked from accessing the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param IssueNumber, the version of the document to reject.
@param RejectComment, a description about why the approval is being rejected.
@return Rejected, '1' if the approval was successfully rejected, otherwise '0'.

Add a meeting note to a document. Must provide either a comment or one
or more attachments. If the list of people to notify includes ones with
limited access then they will not be contacted.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to add meeting notes.
 * The user has limited access to the document.
 * The specified issue does not exist.
 * The specified issue is locked and cannot be changed.
 * Neither a comment or any attachments have been provided.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param IssueNumber, the version number of the document to check.
@param MeetingNote, a note for the meeting.
@param Attachments, a collection of attachment elements. Each attachment must
       consist of an AttachmentData element with the base64 encoded data and
       an AttachmentFilename containing the original filename of the attachment.
@param Notifiers, a collection of Notifier elements, each containing the login of a
       user to notify about the note.
@return NoteAdded, a value of '1' indicates success. If missing then there was an
        error.

This method will add a document to the briefcase.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user is not registered with the system.
 * The user does not permission to access the compartment.
 * The named compartment does not exist.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param Compartment, the name of the location within the briefcase.
@return Added, the name of the compartment that the document was
        added to.

This method will remove the specified document from the user's briefcase.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.
 * No documents were matched.
 * The user does not have permission to access the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to remove.
@param Compartment, the name of the compartment in which the document is located.
@return Removed, with the part number of the document that was removed.

This method will rename a compartment in the user's briefcase.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.
 * The compartment does not exist.
 * No new name was supplied.
 * The user does not have permission to change the name.

@param Compartment, the name of the compartment to change.
@param Name, the new name for the compartment.
@return Compartment, if successful containing the id and new
        name of the compartment.

This method will retrieve the form data for a specified document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * The user does not have permission to use forms.
 * The user does not have permission to access the specified form.

If the user is blocked from accessing the document then an empty collection
will be returned.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document.
@param ReportId, the identity of the report for which the field information is required.
@param ReturnFields, a collection of ReturnField elements containing the names of the
       fields to return.
@return A collection of Field elements containing the form id, field id and value of each
        field.

This method will return the identity of a single new task, that is sent to selected users
and/or groups.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * No users or groups have been specified.
 * The type of the task does not exist.
 * The specified task type is not one that is active.
 * The due date was not in the correct format or not valid.
 * The due date is in the past.
 * The user does not have permission to use tasks.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to raise the request for.
@param TaskTypeId, the task type to use.
@param DueDate, an optional date that the task should be completed by, in YYYY-MM-DD format.
@param Comment, a description of the task that is sent with the task request to the users.
@param Users, the set of logins to send the request to.
@param Groups, the set of numeric group identities to send the request to.
@return TaskRequestId, the identity of the new task request. Together with Users,
        the logins of the people that the task has been assigned to.

This method will cancel the request to perform a task.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.

@param TaskRequestId, the identity of the task request.
@param Comment, an optional description of why the task request is being cancelled.
@return Cancelled, '1' if the task request was cancelled, otherwise '0'.

This method will accept an existing task request.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.
 * The task request does not exist.

@param TaskRequestId, the identity of the task request to accept.
@param Comment, an optional description about accepting the task.
@return Accepted, '1' if the task was successfully accepted, otherwise '0'.
        TaskId, the identity of the task that was accepted.

This method will cancel an existing task.

The method will fail if:

 * The task does not exist.
 * The user is not registered with the system.
 * The user is unable to cancel the task.
 * The user is not registered with the system.

@param TaskId, the identity of the task.
@param Comment, an optional description about why the task is being cancelled.
@return Cancelled, '1' if the task was cancelled, otherwise '0'.

This method will change the state of the specified task.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.

@param TaskId, the identity of the task.
@param TaskStateId, the identity of the state that the task should be set to.
@param Comment, an optional description as to why the state changed.
@return Changed, '1' if the state changed, otherwise '0'. TaskStateId
        containing the current identity of the state of the task.

This method will create and return the identity of the first new task for a document. After the
tasks have been created then notifications are sent to the selected users.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.
 * No user logins were provided.
 * The identity of the task type is missing or is not valid.
 * The task type is one that is not currently active.
 * The due date is not in the correct format.
 * The due date is in the past.
 * The user does not have permission to use tasks.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document to create the task for.
@param TaskTypeId, the task type to use.
@param DueDate, the date the task is due by, in YYYY-MM-DD format.
@param Comment, a description about the task that is sent to the users.
@param Users, a collection of logins to send the request to.
@return TaskId, the identity of the newly created task.

This method will move a task from one user to another.

The method will fail if:

 * The user is not registered with the system.

@param TaskId, the identity of the task to change.
@param Assignee, the login of the person to assign the task to.
@param Comment, an optional description as to the reason for the change.
@return Changed, '1' if the task was re-assigned, otherwise '0'.

This method will retrieve all of the pre-filter data that would be applied to
a document.

The method will fail if:

 * The document does not exist.

If either of the following occurs, then no information is returned.

 * The user is not registered with the system.
 * The user has been blocked from accessing the document.

@param PartNumber, the identity of the document for which the data is to be fetched.
@param IssueNumber, the version of the document.
@param IssueType, the type i.e. 'draft' or 'issue'
@return Properties, a collection of Property elements containing name/value pairs of
        the pre-filter data that can be added to a document. This includes such data
        as CogniDox_Partnum, CogniDox_Title, CogniDox_Version etc.
